{
    "note": "What convert_frigates.py needs to know about each new frigate model (the recoloured copies in ai models/retextured, made by recolour_frigate.py). Positions are in the GLB's coordinates after Blender's import: bow at -X, +Z up, the hull on z = 0, 1 unit long; boxes are [x0, x1, y0, y1, z0, z1]. The \"ships\" (destroyers and the cruiser, built at shipyards) are the same, with a prefix for their files, extra_mounts (ball-mounted guns added on the hull: a point and the side it faces) and missile_cells (launch cells on the deck); their GLBs were aligned with align_glb.py. A turret is the parts of the model inside its boxes, cut out so they can turn: its barrels (loose parts whose middle is in the barrels box) elevate, the rest (the housing) traverses. A housing_mode of faces takes every face in the box (not whole loose parts): for a housing joined to its twin across the hull. A barrel_faces box (or list of boxes) adds barrels modelled joined to their housing: the pieces (between UV seams) of the housing's parts lying wholly in it elevate with the barrels. Read off grid_glb.py, grid_end.py and islands_render.py renders.",
